  "text": {
    "intro": "Six makers press in six different months and each is privately certain the others have let theirs go to vinegar.\nFour makers are involved. Determine each maker's pressing month, vessel and fault.\n- **Maker**: Silas Vane, Bryony, Jethro and Araminta.\n- **Pressing month** (listed from earlier to later): January, February, March and April.\n- **Vessel**: a sherry butt, a rum cask, a stainless tank and an oak hogshead.\n- **Fault**: a stuck ferment, sulphur, nothing detectable and acetification.\nEvery maker has a different pressing month, vessel and fault, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "The maker who is accused of acetification presses in January.",
      "Bryony presses in April.",
      "Araminta is accused of nothing detectable. Araminta is exactly one month earlier than the maker who ferments in an oak hogshead, with no pressing month in between.",
      "The maker who ferments in a rum cask is later than March in pressing month order.",
      "The maker who ferments in a stainless tank is exactly one month earlier than the maker who is accused of a stuck ferment, with no pressing month in between.",
      "Jethro is exactly one month earlier than the maker who ferments in a rum cask, with no pressing month in between."
